.TH SDE-GALLERY 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sde-gallery \- browse the photo library on the SDE desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sde-gallery
[\-\-select FILE] [\-\-version | \-\-help]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Gallery shows the pictures in your XDG Pictures folder (see
.BR xdg-user-dir (1))
and in folders you add, grouped by month of their modification time.
The sidebar offers All Photos, Favorites, Recent (the last 30 days),
Screenshots (the Screenshots folder inside Pictures), the folder list and,
under
.BR Devices ,
the cameras, SD cards, USB drives and other removable media mounted below
.I /media
or
.IR /run/media .
The device list follows
.I /proc/self/mountinfo
and changes as media are connected and removed.
A device can be browsed in place, imported, or ejected (the button shown
when the pointer is over it, or its context menu).
JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP and SVG files are shown; WebP, TIFF, AVIF, HEIF and
JPEG XL are shown when the matching gdk-pixbuf loaders are installed.
Photos are shown upright following their EXIF orientation.
.PP
Thumbnails are made in the background and shared with other applications
through the freedesktop.org thumbnail cache in
.IR ~/.cache/thumbnails/normal
and
.IR ~/.cache/thumbnails/large .
.SS Menus
.TP
.B File
Open File (opens it in Photo), Open Folder (browse any folder without
adding it), Import from Device, Add Folder to Library, Refresh, Quit.
.TP
.B Edit
Select All, Select None, Add to Favorites, Copy Path, Move to Trash, Open
in Photo, Set as Wallpaper, Show in Files.
.TP
.B View
Sort order, thumbnail size, Show Sidebar, Open Photos in Photo, Full
Screen.
.TP
.B Help
Keyboard Shortcuts, About Gallery.
.SS Import
Import from Device copies the photos of a device (or the selected ones)
to
.IR ~/Pictures/Imported/YYYY-MM-DD/ ,
the date being the day each photo was taken by the camera (its
modification time). Photos imported before (same name and size) are
skipped; other name clashes get a number, as in
.IR "DSC_0001 (2).JPG" .
.SS Photo
Double-click a photo or press Enter to open the built-in viewer, or, with
.B View > Open Photos in Photo
set, Photo
.RB ( sde-view (1)).
Ctrl+E always opens the photo in Photo. Gallery starts Photo with
.BI \-\-album= ID
and the current sort order, so that Photo steps through the same photos in
the same order (search results are passed as a list). Edits, favorites,
deletions and new files made in Photo appear in Gallery at once; Photo's
.B Show in Gallery
selects the photo in the running Gallery.
.PP
Files are never deleted permanently: Move to Trash uses the
freedesktop.org Trash through GIO.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Arrows, Page Up/Down, Home, End
Move between photos. Shift extends the selection.
.TP
.B Ctrl+click, Shift+click, Space, Ctrl+A, Esc
Select photos, select all, clear the selection.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the photo.
.TP
.B + \- , Ctrl+mouse wheel
Change the thumbnail size (zoom in the viewer).
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Shift+O, Ctrl+I, F5
Search, open a photo, open a folder, import from a device, reload.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+E, Delete
Toggle favorite, copy paths, open in Photo, move to the Trash.
.TP
.B F1, F9, F11, Ctrl+Q
Keyboard shortcuts, sidebar, full screen, quit.
.TP
.B Viewer: 0, 1, R, I, F5, F11, Esc
Fit, actual size, rotate, details, slideshow, full screen, back.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-select " FILE"
Show and select
.IR FILE .
When Gallery is already running, the running window does it and is
raised; only one Gallery runs per display.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Section
.B [gallery]
keeps
.BR folders= ,
.BR favorites=
(lists separated by semicolons),
.BR thumbnail_size= ,
.BR sort= ,
.B sidebar=
and
.BR open_in_photo= .
Set as Wallpaper writes
.B wallpaper=
in
.BR [appearance] .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sde-view (1),
.BR liria (1),
.BR sde-settings (1),
.BR xdg-user-dir (1)
